# Tracer: Template-defined one-based sequence family
#
# Before (did not work):
# template<S set>:
#     have sequence set = fn(n N+) S
# \sequence<R> = fn(n N+) R
# Former behavior: Litex verified the source, but the direct Result-to-Lean compiler rejected DefTemplateStmt.
#
# Now (verified):
template<S set>:
    have sequence set = fn(n N+) S

\sequence<R> = fn(n N+) R
\sequence<R> = \sequence<R>
# Current behavior: the Template definition, first Created instance, Reused instance, and
# exact public equality all verify; the generated Lean family is Litex.fnSet Litex.NPos S.
# The runtime-only boundary probe `0 ∉ N+` is recorded in the adjacent proof journal.
#
# Boundary: this compiler slice rejects template domains, non-set parameters, and non-set-alias bodies.
# It also preserves N+ as the index carrier; it does not translate the family to Lean's zero-based Seq.
# Evidence: target/release/litex -graph -f lean/examples/55_TemplateSequenceInstantiationResult.lit
# Compiler: target/release/stmt_result_to_lean_compiler compile lean/examples/55_TemplateSequenceInstantiationResult.lit
# Lean: cd lean && lake env lean examples/55_TemplateSequenceInstantiationResult.lean
